{"name":"Matador’s Cape","hex":"#cf6e66","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"matador","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The person whose aim is to kill the bull in a bullfight.","A certain game of dominoes in which four dominoes (the 4-3, 5-2, 6-1, and double blank), called matadors, may be played at any time in any way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/matador"},{"term":"cape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece or point of land, extending beyond the adjacent coast into a sea or lake; a promontory; a headland."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sleeveless garment or part of a garment, hanging from the neck over the back, arms, and shoulders.","A superhero."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cape"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cape","blocks":[{"text":"A cape is a clothing accessory or a sleeveless outer garment of any length that hangs loosely and connects either at the neck or shoulders. They usually cover the back, shoulders, and arms. They come in a variety of styles and have been used throughout history for many different reasons."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape","wikidata":"Q1034198"},{"title":"Bullfighter","blocks":[{"text":"A bullfighter or matador is a performer in the activity of bullfighting. Torero or toureiro, both from Latin taurarius, are the Spanish and Portuguese words for bullfighter, and describe all the performers in the activity of bullfighting as practised in Spain, Portugal, Mexico, Peru, France, Colombia, Ecuador, Venezuela and other countries influenced by Portuguese and Spanish culture. The main performer and leader of the entourage in a bullfight, and who finally kills the bull, is addressed as maestro (master), or with the formal title matador de toros. The other bullfighters in the entourage are called subalternos and their suits are embroidered in silver as opposed to the matador's gold. They include the picadores, rejoneadores, and banderilleros."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Corrida%2C_Rio_Lagartos%2C_Yucatan.jpg/330px-Corrida%2C_Rio_Lagartos%2C_Yucatan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bullfighter","wikidata":"Q549322"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Batman_and_Robin_1966.JPG/500px-Batman_and_Robin_1966.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Batman_and_Robin_1966.JPG/500px-Batman_and_Robin_1966.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Batman and Robin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABatman_and_Robin_1966.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Dracula_Cape.jpg/120px-Dracula_Cape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Dracula_Cape.jpg/250px-Dracula_Cape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Dracula_Cape.jpg/120px-Dracula_Cape.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADracula_Cape.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Nezahualpiltzintli.jpg/120px-Nezahualpiltzintli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Nezahualpiltzintli.jpg/250px-Nezahualpiltzintli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Nezahualpiltzintli.jpg/120px-Nezahualpiltzintli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia